{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And sometimes the cloud would be from evening until morning.</b> He describes a fourth possibility: that sometimes the cloud's encampment lasted an immeasurable time — only a single night — which is a span insufficiently prepared for the needs of encampment and for the needs of travel. Yet along with this, he notes that no journey ever began at night."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:11.019123819Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}